    "result_text": "Each claim now shows its status log, and `bin/e2e` passes (1 test).\n\nEach line reads `<STATUS> by <user> on <date> due=<due>`, oldest first, shown under the claim as `claim-log-line` elements. The due is the claim's due computed on the server at the moment of the change, so later rate changes don't alter old lines. If no rate applied at that moment, the line shows `due=n/a`.\n\n**Stored data:** a new migration, `V23__claim_log.sql`, adds a `claim_log` table holding the status, user, sheet's today and due for each line. Claims that already exist start with an empty log, since there's no record of their past statuses.\n\n**Server:**\n- A claim now remembers the status it was loaded with. After a save, `SaveClaim` writes a log line if the status has changed. A new claim has no loaded status, so adding one writes its DRAFT line.\n- Because every action goes through `SaveClaim`, open, settle, pending, approve, reject, void and quick-add are all logged. Bulk open saves claims itself, so I added logging there too. Edits and moving a claim to another person don't change the status, so they write nothing.\n- A refused change never reaches the save step, so it writes no log line.\n- Claim responses now include a `log` list. The sheet's claim list loads all the log lines for the sheet in one query.\n\n**Front end:** the `Claim` type gains the `log` field, and the claim row in `claims.slot.tsx` lists the lines.\n\nThe audit file is unchanged: the spec expects no audit records for this change.",
